.TH COMPLIANCE\-EVIDENCE 1 "2026-11-04" "unheaded b34c6069" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
compliance\-evidence \- Collect compliance evidence (gates, CI runs, host facts) into the evidence file; subcommands render findings, SSPs, snapshots and Ansible.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B compliance\-evidence
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
[COMMAND]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Collect compliance evidence (gates, CI runs, host facts) into the evidence file; subcommands render findings, SSPs, snapshots and Ansible.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B findings
findings register from the catalog
.TP
.B ssp
system security plan
.TP
.B snapshot
sealed baseline snapshot
.TP
.B ansible
render Ansible from the catalog
.TP
.B profile
control profiles in the Well
.TP
.B well
sync the catalog into the Well
.TP
.B baseline
host baseline
.TP
.B wire
wire compliance plane, off unless \-\-serve (ADR\-127)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-branch \fISTRING\fR
branch whose CI runs are evidence (default develop)
.TP
.B \-\-github\-repo \fISTRING\fR
owner/name for GitHub Actions evidence (default unheaded/unheaded)
.TP
.B \-\-keep \fIN\fR
records kept per source (default 50)
.TP
.B \-\-out \fISTRING\fR
evidence file to merge into (default var/compliance/evidence.json)
.TP
.B \-\-repo\-dir \fISTRING\fR
repository root (catalog, git, scripts/) (default .)
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-gates
do not run gate scripts
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
